HATE EQUALITY
Key Logic
->If all characters in S are the same, then any shuffle of T will still be identical to S → return 0
->If at least two different characters exist, you can rearrange them to form a different string → return 1
->If N = 1, only one permutation exists → return 0

CODE IN JAVA

public class Solution {

    public static int canYouMakeDifference(int n, String s) {
        if (n == 1) {
            return 0;
        }
        char first = s.charAt(0);
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (s.charAt(i) != first) {
                return 1;
            }
        }
        return 0;
    }
}
